  "debrief": "A transistor switch must be driven into saturation: enough base current that β × I_B is well above what the load needs, so the load, not the transistor, sets the current. 10 kΩ gives 0.83 mA, room for 166 mA, so the 43 mA of LEDs light fully. With 47 kΩ it can only pass 35 mA and every LED dims."
